# Byte-code caches. Tracked by accident before this file existed, and
# `git rm --cached` on them was part of adding it: a .pyc changes on
# every run, so it puts a line in every diff and buries the source
# change that was actually made.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The environment and the runner's own state. `uv` rebuilds the first
# from uv.lock; the second is the pytest run's, and neither is a fact
# about the project.
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# The graph and the conversations. product.md: "A graph is derived and
# disposable" and "A session writes nothing into the branch, and is kept
# outside it, since what it records is note content" — so a store is
# something a branch produces where it is run, never something committed
# beside the code.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
